      "avalancheActivity": {
        "comment": "The main issue is fresh snow at the highest elevations. We expect 10\u201315 cm of fresh snow. Be cautious in very steep areas, narrow gullies, slopes beneath rock faces, and terrain depressions where snow has been blown by the wind into snow pillows, slabs, and drifts. Prolonged low temperatures and a thin snowpack are leading to the development of critical\u2014permanently weak\u2014layers within the snowpack. Avalanches may be triggered primarily by significant additional loading, though the occurrence of smaller spontaneous avalanches from fresh snow cannot be ruled out.",
