      "snowpackStructure": {
        "comment": "Cold air of Arctic origin continues to linger over Slovakia, bringing snowfall from the north accompanied by strong NW to S winds. Over the past 3 days, 10 to 30 cm of new snow has fallen; a continuous snowpack is present starting from the foothills, with significant depths found above the tree line, where it reaches 30 to 70 cm, and locally even more. Partly due to low temperatures, the snow layers are not sufficiently bonded together. Due to the wind, the snow cover is distributed very unevenly."
